Ladybird processes a document’s Link header preloads before the
document is its navigable’s active document, and answers if their
requests have a cross-site ancestor for the navigable being navigated.
Blink only issues them after the commit, in DocumentLoader::
CreateParserPostCommit(), and computes the network isolation of a
pending commit from the navigating frame, in RenderFrameHostImpl::
ComputeIsolationInfoForSubresourcesForPendingCommit(). WebKit issues
them from FrameLoader::receivedFirstData(), once LocalFrame::
setDocument() has installed the new document. And Gecko issues them
through PreloadService::PreloadLinkHeader() with the new document as
the loading context, which is first-party for a top-level window. So
all three send a same-site page’s cookies with them.
